# OPTIONAL. Nothing here is required: `docker compose up -d` works with no .env at all.
# To change a setting, put its line in a file called .env beside docker-compose.yml
# (docker compose reads it automatically; ./setup-dirs.sh --migrate reads it too).

# THREE volumes make it work: config, catalog, and your media.
#
# One LOCAL folder holds the first two. LOCAL DISK, never an SMB/CIFS share (the database
# misbehaves over one, and the symlinks don't work):
#   config/    everything the container keeps: runtime/ (FieldStation42's sqlite schedule
#              database and sockets), confs/ (station configs), tuner/ (the dashboard's config),
#              and your groups.toml
#   catalog/   everything made of symlinks: by-genre/ (the tag folders), media-links/ (a symlink
#              for every video on your media)
# (This was called FS42_SSD_ROOT. Rename it, then run ./setup-dirs.sh --migrate to move an
#  existing install into this layout.)
# Default: a folder called data beside docker-compose.yml.
# FS42_LOCAL_ROOT=/srv/station-wrapper-43

# Your media: the one thing that SHOULD be on your NAS. Mounted read-only at /mnt/media, and the
# symlinks point into it, so it must be mounted at the same path in the container.
# By default the whole folder is shared in, and shares mounted INSIDE it (/mnt/media/tv from one
# NAS, /mnt/media/movies from another) show up too.
# To share in only SOME folders (/mnt/media/youtube, /mnt/media/anime, /mnt/media/movies), use one
# line per folder instead: see "ONLY SOME FOLDERS" in docker-compose.yml.
# Default: a folder called media beside docker-compose.yml. This is the one line most installs set.
# FS42_MEDIA_ROOT=/mnt/media

# Move one of the two local volumes somewhere else on LOCAL disk (each defaults to a folder under
# FS42_LOCAL_ROOT):
# FS42_CONFIG_ROOT=/srv/station-wrapper-43/config
# FS42_CATALOG_ROOT=/srv/station-wrapper-43/catalog
# The container refuses to start if the config or the catalog is on SMB or can't hold a symlink
# (exit 78). Only for a share you have TESTED, set this to 1 to start anyway:
# FS42_ALLOW_NETWORK_CATALOG=1

# Image tag to pull from ghcr.io/austincnunn: latest (the default), main-<short-sha> to pin one build,
# dev, or a release version such as 0.1.0.
# FS42_TAG=latest

# Everything runs in ONE container. The console and the dashboard always run. Two more
# things inside it are switched on here (leave them off if you don't want them):

# -- farm: ON by default. Keeps catalog/by-genre filled with tag folders of links (genres from the
#    NFO files, Unclassified, bump) so FieldStation42's console
#    has something to build stations from. Add-only; it does not create stations.
# FARM_ENABLED=0
# FARM_INTERVAL_MINUTES=30

# -- test station: ON by default. A brand new install (no stations yet) gets "Test Pattern" on
#    channel 0, a test card with a quiet tone, so the dashboard shows something at once and you
#    can see the whole chain works. It happens once; delete it in the console and it stays gone.
# FIRSTRUN_TEST_STATION=0
# FIRSTRUN_CLIP_SECONDS=60

# -- weather channel: OFF by default. This line starts the two small containers at the bottom of docker-compose.yml, which draw a
#    WeatherStar 4000 forecast, and adds it as a channel (channel 3, or the next free number), on a new install or an
#    old one. Then: docker compose up -d. The place is set on the dashboard's Settings page (a ZIP code, or City, State;
#    United States only); WEATHER_LOCATION here is only its starting value.
#    Why off: the hidden browser that draws it runs all day (about one CPU core and 1 GB of memory), and it exists for
#    amd64 machines only, so not on a Raspberry Pi or other ARM machine.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=weather
# WEATHER_LOCATION=20001

# -- schedule keeper: ON by default. FieldStation42 only extends a station's schedule inside its
#    on-screen player, which this container doesn't run, so without this every station goes off air
#    when its scheduled days run out. It tops each station that has a schedule up to KEEPER_DAYS_AHEAD
#    days, adding days only (never rebuilding). Change it on the Stations page; these are only the
#    starting values.
# SCHEDULE_KEEPER=0
# KEEPER_DAYS_AHEAD=7
# KEEPER_INTERVAL_MINUTES=30

# -- the dashboard login: ON by default. The first visit to a management page asks you to set a
#    password (whoever gets there first sets it, so do it straight away). Or set it here: it is used
#    only if no password has been set yet. DASHBOARD_LOGIN=0 switches the login off, for anyone
#    who puts their own login in front. The player and the guide/lineup other clients use stay open;
#    FieldStation42's own console on port 4242 is NOT covered by it.
# DASHBOARD_LOGIN=0
# DASHBOARD_PASSWORD=

# -- the web viewer: OFF unless a port is set here (and published in the compose file's ports). It
#    serves the player alone on that port. Each viewer logs in with a name and password and gets
#    only the channels picked for them on the Settings page (the Viewers tab). Port 5004 still lets
#    anyone watch every channel, so give viewers this port only (a reverse proxy or a firewall).
# VIEWER_PORT=5005

# -- FieldStation42's console (port 4242) has no login, so it answers only on the server itself
#    (http://localhost:4242, or through an SSH tunnel). 0.0.0.0 opens it to your network: the
#    dashboard's console links then work from other machines. Never publish it to the internet.
# FS42_CONSOLE_BIND=0.0.0.0

# -- the Lists & files tab of Settings (http://<host>:5004/settings.html#files) builds your lists (tag folders) of links.
#    Behind the login (below). 0 = look-only even when logged in.
# DASHBOARD_EDIT=1

# -- sync: keeps the pool (catalog/media-links) current and watches the tag folders -----
# SYNC_ENABLED=1
# Every SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES it adds a symlink for each new video on the share.
# It never removes or rewrites a link.
# SYNC_INTERVAL_MINUTES=60
# A full walk of the share now and then, in case the server doesn't update folder times:
# SYNC_FULL_EVERY_HOURS=24
# Only some libraries: top-level folder names under FS42_MEDIA_ROOT, comma-separated.
# SYNC_INCLUDE=tvseries,movies
# SYNC_EXCLUDE=downloads
# Remove pool links whose file is gone from the share (off: nothing is ever removed):
# SYNC_PRUNE=1
# A link you copy into a tag folder isn't seen until that station's catalog is updated. Once a day,
# starting at SYNC_REBUILD_HOUR (local time) and within SYNC_REBUILD_WINDOW_HOURS of it, the stations whose
# lists changed get their catalogs updated with the new videos. Their schedules are NOT touched: the new
# videos are used the next time days are added (the schedule keeper does that each morning):
# SYNC_REBUILD=1                 # on by default; set 0 to only report what changed
# SYNC_REBUILD_HOUR=4
# SYNC_REBUILD_WINDOW_HOURS=2

# -- Emby or Jellyfin (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# The guide's names, episode titles, synopses, air dates and posters, from the media server that already knows your
# library (its metadata is in its database, not in .nfo files). Either server works; which one is detected. Off unless
# both are set. The key: Emby: Dashboard > Advanced > API Keys; Jellyfin: Dashboard > API Keys.
# MEDIA_SERVER_URL=http://192.168.1.20:8096
# MEDIA_SERVER_API_KEY=
# The folder the SERVER sees your media in (the same files as FS42_MEDIA_ROOT, maybe under another path):
# MEDIA_SERVER_MEDIA_ROOT=/media

# ---- Read-ahead (so a slow network share doesn't make a viewer wait) ----------------------------------------
# For each channel being watched, the NEXT thing to play (the commercial break while a show plays, the next episode
# while a break plays) is copied into a RAM disk before it is due, and the tuner plays the copy. It learns how fast
# each share is and starts early enough. The share is only read; nothing is written to a drive.
# PREFETCH=1                  # on by default; 0 turns it off
# PREFETCH_CACHE_SIZE=6g      # the RAM disk's size (the compose file's tmpfs line); it counts against Docker's memory
# PREFETCH_MAX_MB=5400        # how much of it to use (keep this a little under the size above)
# To use a folder on DISK instead of RAM (some machines have more disk than RAM): remove the tmpfs line from the
# compose file, mount a local folder, and set
# PREFETCH_RAM=0
# PREFETCH_DIR=/cache         # the folder, as the container sees it

